<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2182 0 R
/E (Your content sounds different every week. Your LinkedIn posts, website copy, and email newsletters feel like they were written by three different people. You can't brief a writer or a VA because you can't describe your voice.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
2742 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2182 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
2743 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2182 0 R
/E (Brand voice is the consistent personality and tone your brand uses across all communications. It is not the same as tone: tone adjusts to context \(a sales email is more direct than a thought leadership post\), but voice stays constant. A strong brand voice has three layers: Personality Traits \(the adjectives that describe how you sound\), Voice Rules \(what you do and don't say\), and Tone Variations \(how the voice shifts across contexts\). When your voice is defined, every piece of content, even AI-generated sounds unmistakably like you.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
2744 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14133 0 R
/E ( Define your voice by what you are and what you are not  the contrast sharpens the definition.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
