>>
endobj
2808 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2184 0 R
/E (A Growth Loop is a self-reinforcing system where each user or customer generates the conditions for the next. Unlike a funnel \(linear, ends at conversion\), a loop feeds itself. The four types are: Viral Loop \(users invite others\), Content Loop \(content generates SEO or social reach that drives new users\), Paid Loop \(revenue from users funds ads that acquire more users\), and Product Loop \(using the product creates value that is visible to non-users\). Andrew Chen and Brian Balfour popularised growth loops as the foundation of sustainable, compounding growth.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
