2876 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2186 0 R
/E (Find where your growth is actually leaking)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
2877 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2186 0 R
/E (You're investing in marketing and the numbers aren't moving. Or you have users but no revenue. Or you have revenue but high churn. You don't know which stage of your funnel is broken because you're not measuring them separately.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
2878 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2186 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
2879 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2186 0 R
/E (Created by Dave McClure of 500 Startups in 2007, AARRR maps the five stages of growth: Acquisition \(how users find you\), Activation \(when they first experience value\), Retention \(whether they come back\), Revenue \(how you make money from them\), and Referral \(whether they tell others\). Most companies measure only Acquisition and Revenue  the middle three stages are where the real insight and the real growth leaks are. Improving any single stage by 10% compounds across the entire funnel.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
2880 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14174 0 R
/E (Map your current metrics for all five stages before analysing  you can't fix what you don't measure.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
2881 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14175 0 R
/E (Identify the stage with the largest drop-off  that is your biggest growth lever.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
2882 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14176 0 R
/E (Fix the weakest stage before investing more in Acquisition more traffic into a broken funnel wastes money.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
2883 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14177 0 R
/E (Define one specific metric per stage and review weekly.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
