2944 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2188 0 R
/E (Jim Collins introduced the Flywheel concept in Good to Great \(2001\) as a metaphor for business momentum. A flywheel takes enormous effort to start spinning but gains momentum with every rotation until it becomes self-sustaining. Amazon's flywheel is the most famous example: lower prices attract more customers, who attract more sellers, who drive lower costs, which enable lower prices. Every business has the potential for a flywheel  the question is whether you've designed it deliberately. AI can help you identify and map yours.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
