3032 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2191 0 R
/E (RACI defines four roles for every task or decision: Responsible \(does the work\), Accountable \(owns the outcome - one person only\), Consulted \(gives input before action\), Informed \(told after action\). The single most important rule: there must be exactly one Accountable person per task. When two people are accountable, nobody is accountable. When this matrix is applied to your team's key processes, task duplication drops, decision speed increases, and your inbox stops filling with questions that aren't yours to answer.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
