3290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2199 0 R
/E (You avoid giving difficult feedback because it always turns into a difficult conversation. Or you give feedback that the person defends against instead of hears. The problem stays the same, the conversation gets harder each time.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
3291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2199 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
3292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2199 0 R
/E (Developed by the Center for Creative Leadership, the SBI model structures feedback across three elements: Situation \(the specific context , when and where\), Behaviour \(the observable action, what you saw or heard, not your interpretation\), and Impact \(the effect the behaviour had on you, the team, or the outcome\). SBI removes the most common feedback failure modes: vague generalisations \('you're not a team player'\), character judgements \('you're disorganised'\), and assumed intent \('you clearly don't care'\). AI can help you convert a difficult feedback situation into a clean SBI statement.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
3293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14305 0 R
/E (Write the Behaviour in observable terms only  what you could have filmed, not what you interpreted.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
3294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14306 0 R
/E (State the Impact from your perspective,  'I felt' or 'the team experienced' - not 'you caused.')
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
