3499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2205 0 R
/E (Drawing from Patrick Lencioni's work on organisational health and broader meeting efficiency research, the Meeting OS is a set of design principles for every recurring and ad hoc meeting: define the meeting type \(decision, discussion, update, or brainstorm\), set the agenda 24 hours in advance, start with the most important item first, assign one facilitator, end with explicit decisions and owners recorded, and send a summary within an hour. AI can design a complete meeting operating system for any team structure.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
