/P 2209 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
3640 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2209 0 R
/E (Hoshin Kanri \(Japanese: direction management\) is a strategic planning and execution framework developed in Japan in the 1950s, refined at Toyota and Bridgestone, and adopted by many Fortune 500 companies. It cascades organisational objectives through every level of the company using a 'catchball' process goals are thrown back and forth between leadership and teams until both sides agree on what is achievable and how it connects. The result is a company where every person's daily work is visibly connected to the company's annual and long-term goals.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
