3702 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2211 0 R
/E (Developed by Paul Hersey and Ken Blanchard in 1969, Situational Leadership proposes that no single leadership style works for all people in all situations. Effective leadership adapts to two variables: the team member's Competence \(knowledge and skill for the specific task\) and Commitment \(motivation and confidence\). The four resulting styles are: Directing \(high task, low support for low competence, high commitment\), Coaching \(high task, high support  for some competence, variable commitment\), Supporting \(low task, high support for high competence, low confidence\), and Delegating \(low task, low support for high competence, high commitment\).)
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
3703 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14436 0 R
