3766 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2213 0 R
/E (You've made a strategic shift  new direction, new structure, new hires but results aren't following. Something is misaligned but you can't identify what. The strategy is clear but the execution keeps resisting it.)
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
3767 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2213 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
3768 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2213 0 R
/E (Developed by McKinsey consultants Tom Peters and Robert Waterman in 1980, the 7S Framework maps seven interdependent elements of an organisation that must all be aligned for strategy to work. The Hard Ss - Strategy \(plan\), Structure \(org chart\), Systems \(processes and IT\) are the visible elements. The Soft Ss - Shared Values \(culture and beliefs\), Skills \(capabilities\), Style \(leadership approach\), Staff \(people\) - are invisible but often more powerful. When any element is misaligned with the others, change stalls. AI can run a 7S diagnostic on your business and identify where the friction lives.)
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [7]
