4278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2228 0 R
/E (Your team is building something a product, a feature, a process, a service  and the conversation keeps starting with what you have, what you can build, or what technology allows. You need to reverse the direction of thinking before a single hour of work is spent.your team spends hours every week on tasks that are repetitive, rule-based, and predictable. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
4279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2228 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
4280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2228 0 R
/E (Developed by Jeff Bezos and embedded into Amazon's culture, Working Backwards begins at the end: the customer experience. Before any project starts, the team writes a mock Press Release announcing the finished product from the customer's point of view. It must answer: Who is the customer? What is their problem? Why is this meaningfully better than before? If the press release cannot be written clearly, the project is not ready to start. Amazon used this to build Prime, Alexa, AWS, and the Kindle  each beginning with a customer document, not a technology roadmap. What looks like a writing exercise is a decision filter. Projects that cannot survive it should not be started.)
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
4281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14612 0 R
/E (Start with the highest-frequency tasks  daily tasks with 10 minutes of work are worth more to automate than monthly tasks with 2 hours.)
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
4282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14613 0 R
/E (Never automate a broken process, fix the process first, then automate it.)
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
