>>
endobj
4340 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2230 0 R
/E (Developed from Jeff Sutherland and Ken Schwaber's Scrum framework, the Sprint Canvas is a one-page planning tool for a two-week sprint. It maps: Sprint Goal \(the one thing that defines success for this sprint\), Backlog Items \(tasks selected to achieve the goal\), Dependencies \(what needs to happen before these tasks can start\), Risks \(what could prevent completion\), Definition of Done \(how we know each item is complete\), and Daily Standup Questions \(what keeps the team aligned\). AI can help design a sprint that is internally coherent, where every backlog item connects to the sprint goal.)
/Pg 71 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
