4558 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2236 0 R
/E (Poka-Yoke \(Japanese: poka = inadvertent mistake, yoke = prevent\) was developed by Shigeo Shingo at Toyota in the 1960s. The principle is to design processes, tools, and environments so that errors either cannot occur or are immediately detected and corrected before they cause damage. There are two types: Prevention Poka-Yoke \(makes the mistake physically or logically impossible\) and Detection Poka-Yoke \(catches the error immediately after it occurs, before it passes forward\). Applied to business processes and digital workflows, Poka-Yoke reduces the reliance on human vigilance and builds quality into the system itself.)
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
