4622 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2238 0 R
/E (The 5 Whys was developed by Sakichi Toyoda, the founder of Toyota Industries, as a simple but powerful root cause analysis technique. When a problem occurs, ask Why it happened. Take that answer and ask Why again. Repeat five times. By the fifth Why, you have typically arrived at the systemic root cause not the visible symptom. The technique is deceptively simple: most people stop at the first or second Why, fix the symptom, and wonder why the problem returns. )
/Pg 79 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
4623 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2238 0 R
/E (The chain only holds if each answer is something you can actually verify, not a guess dressed up as an explanation. A fifth Why built on four assumptions gives you a confident-sounding root cause that is still wrong.)
/Pg 79 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
4624 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2238 0 R
/E (A problem keeps coming back after you fix it. You treat the visible issue and it reappears in a different form. Your team is busy fixing the same category of problem repeatedly without eliminating it.)
/Pg 79 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
