/E (A structured six-step process for any decision that matters)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
4716 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2241 0 R
/E (You are going in circles on an important decision. You have information but can't reach clarity. The same arguments keep coming up. You need a process to move from deliberation to decision.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
4717 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2241 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
4718 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2241 0 R
/E (The DECIDE framework, developed in decision science, is a six-step structured decision process: Define the problem \(what exactly are you deciding?\), Establish criteria \(what does a good decision look like?\), Consider alternatives \(what are all the realistic options?\), Identify the best option \(evaluate alternatives against criteria\), Develop and implement \(commit and plan\), Evaluate the outcome \(review after the fact\). Its value is in making implicit decision-making explicit  surfacing the criteria and alternatives that are often left unstated, which is where most poor decisions hide.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
4719 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14729 0 R
/E (Define the decision in one sentence before doing anything else  ambiguous definition is the root of most decision paralysis.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
4720 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14730 0 R
/E (Write your criteria before generating options  criteria set after options are considered are reverse-engineered rationalisations.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
4721 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14731 0 R
/E (Generate at least three alternatives  binary choices limit thinking.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
4722 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14732 0 R
/E (Set a decision date before starting the process. Open-ended decision timelines produce no decisions.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
4723 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2241 0 R
/E <4F726967696E3A204465636973696F6E20736369656E6365206D6574686F646F6C6F6779208420444543494445206672616D65776F726B2C204B72697374696E612047756F20616E64206F7468657273>
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
4724 0 obj
<<
