4846 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2245 0 R
/E (Extract the full learning from every outcome - win or lose)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
4847 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2245 0 R
/E (Your team debriefs informally after projects finish. The same mistakes recur because learning is not systematically captured or applied. Wins are celebrated without understanding what caused them. You are not compounding your experience.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
4848 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2245 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
4849 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2245 0 R
/E (A Post-Mortem is a structured review conducted after a project, campaign, launch, or significant event to extract learning and improve future performance. Unlike a blame session or a celebration, a well-run Post-Mortem is analytically neutral  it asks what happened, why it happened, and what will be done differently next time. Amazon pioneered the blameless post-mortem culture in engineering; it applies equally to sales, marketing, product, and leadership decisions. AI can structure a complete Post-Mortem analysis when given the outcome data.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
4850 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14777 0 R
/E (Run Post-Mortems on wins as well as failures - understanding what caused a win is equally valuable.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
4851 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14778 0 R
/E (Schedule the Post-Mortem within 2 weeks of the outcome, memory degrades fast.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
4852 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14779 0 R
/E (Focus on process, not people , a good Post-Mortem improves systems, not morale.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
4853 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14780 0 R
/E (The output must include specific changes, a Post-Mortem without action items is a retrospective, not a review.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
