>>
endobj
5178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2255 0 R
/E (Jeff Bezos developed the Regret Minimization Framework when deciding whether to leave his job at D.E. Shaw to start Amazon in 1994. The method is simple: project yourself to age 80, looking back on your life. From that vantage point, ask which choice you would regret more doing it, or not doing it. Bezos found that he would not regret trying and failing, but he would deeply regret never having tried. The framework shifts the decision from short-term risk calculus to long-term life alignment. AI can help you run this thought experiment with structured reflection prompts.)
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
5179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14876 0 R
/E (Use this framework for large, relatively irreversible decisions, not daily choices. )
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
5180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14877 0 R
/E (Be honest in the 80-year-old perspective  romanticised or pessimistic projections both distort the output.)
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
5181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 14878 0 R
/E (Consider both regrets: the regret of action \(if it fails\) and the regret of inaction \(if you never try\).)
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
