/E (The '100 times' question at the end is the most clarifying. EV is a long-run average, it tells you which option wins if you could repeat the decision many times. For irreversible, once-in-a-career decisions, EV is necessary but not sufficient. Pair it with worst-case analysis: can you survive the worst outcome of the highest-EV option? If yes, take it. If no, reconsider.)
/Pg 101 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
