5749 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2274 0 R
/E (Your business metrics are almost entirely financial -  revenue, costs, and margin. But the things that will determine your financial results next year, customer satisfaction, team capability, operational efficiency, innovation pipeline, are not being measured at all.)
/Pg 115 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
5750 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2274 0 R
/E (HOW TO USE IT)
/Pg 115 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
5751 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2274 0 R
/E (Developed by Robert Kaplan and David Norton at Harvard Business School and published in Harvard Business Review in 1992, the Balanced Scorecard measures business performance across four perspectives: Financial \(how do we look to shareholders?\), Customer \(how do customers see us?\), Internal Processes \(what must we excel at?\), and Learning & Growth \(can we continue to improve and create value?\). The insight is that financial metrics are lagging indicators - they tell you what happened. The other three perspectives contain the leading indicators that predict future financial performance.)
/Pg 115 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
5752 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 15071 0 R
/E (Build the scorecard around your strategy, not generic KPIs. Each measure must connect to a strategic objective.)
/Pg 115 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
