5990 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2281 0 R
/E (Applying the SWOT framework to yourself  rather than to a business  creates a structured self-assessment that combines honesty with strategy. Personal Strengths are capabilities and qualities you genuinely have, verified by evidence. Personal Weaknesses are areas where you consistently underperform or avoid. Opportunities are external conditions you could leverage given your specific strengths. Threats are external conditions that specifically threaten you given your specific weaknesses. The strategic output is identifying which strengths to double down on and which weaknesses need a hire, a partner, or deliberate development.)
/Pg 122 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
