/E (You are successful by external measures but unclear on whether you are doing the right work. Or you are considering a major pivot and want to evaluate it against something deeper than market opportunity. You need a framework for purposeful direction, not just profitable direction.)
/Pg 138 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
6515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2297 0 R
/E (Ikigai \(Japanese: iki = life, gai = worth or value\) is a concept from Okinawan philosophy describing the reason for being  the sense of purpose that makes getting up in the morning feel meaningful. In the Western adaptation popularised by Marc Winn and others, Ikigai is visualised as the intersection of four circles: What You Love \(passion\), What You Are Good At \(vocation\), What The World Needs \(mission\), and What You Can Be Paid For \(profession\). The sweet spot at the centre  where all four overlap  is your Ikigai. Applied to a founder's career and business decisions, it is one of the most clarifying frameworks available.)
/Pg 138 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
