/E (Hansei is uncomfortable because it requires taking personal responsibility before assigning external causes. The Western tendency is to explain external causes first and assign personal responsibility last, if at all. Hansei inverts this. The founder who practices it consistently builds a quality of self-awareness that no coaching, therapy, or feedback can replicate because it is chosen and honest.)
/Pg 141 0 R
/K [3]
>>
