endobj
6650 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2301 0 R
/E (Wabi-Sabi is a Japanese aesthetic philosophy rooted in Zen Buddhism that finds beauty in imperfection, impermanence, and incompleteness. Wabi \(rustic simplicity, understated elegance\) and Sabi \(the beauty of aging, the patina of time\) together describe a worldview that accepts  and even celebrates the imperfect and the unfinished as a natural state of all things. Applied to the founder's experience, Wabi-Sabi offers an antidote to perfectionism and a philosophical foundation for the practice of shipping work, releasing versions, and building in public. The product that ships imperfectly and improves beats the product that never ships perfectly. The company itself, like everything else, is a work in progress rather than a finished monument, and that incompleteness is not a flaw to fix but the actual shape of the thing.)
/Pg 142 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
